Step by Step Algorithm:

Step 1: Keep three positions — one at the beginning, one at the current position, and one at the end of the array.
Step 2: Move through the array while the current position does not cross the end position.
Step 3: If the current element is 0, move it to the beginning section and shift both the beginning and current positions forward.
        If the current element is 1, just move the current position forward.
        If the current element is 2, move it to the end section and shift the end position backward.
Step 4: Continue this process until all elements are arranged.
Step 5: At the end, all 0s will be at the start, followed by 1s, and then 2s.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)


-----> Code <----

class Solution {
    public void sortColors(int[] nums) {
        int n=nums.length;
        int st=0,m=0,en=n-1;
        while(m<=en){
            if(nums[m]==1){
                m++;
            }else if(nums[m]==2){
                int temp=nums[m];
                nums[m]=nums[en];
                nums[en]=temp;
                en--;
            }
            else{
                int temp=nums[m];
                nums[m]=nums[st];
                nums[st]=temp;
                st++;
                m++;
            }
        }
        
    }
}
